  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "process_ndpi_collected_info",
    "file": "ndpi/example/reader_util.c",
    "description": "Root cause is a double-free caused by stale ownership of flow->ndpi_flow. In process_ndpi_collected_info(), once detection completes it calls ndpi_free_flow_info_half(flow), which frees flow->ndpi_flow (via ndpi_flow_free -> ndpi_free_flow -> ndpi_free_flow_data) and sets it NULL. However, the same ndpi_flow object is still also owned/referenced elsewhere in the workflow lifecycle and later freed again during flow teardown, leading to invalid free and ASan crash in ndpi_free_flow_data/ndpi_free.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzer input must drive a packet/flow to the detection-complete path in process_ndpi_collected_info() (flow->detection_completed && !flow->check_extra_packets), so ndpi_free_flow_info_half() runs early. Later, normal cleanup (ndpi_tdestroy/flow freer at end of harness iteration) frees the same underlying ndpi_flow again. Crafted PCAP data that reaches this state triggers the second free."
  },
